<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shō En</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1415–1476</span> · Also known as Kanemaru, Sho En</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shō En, born Kanemaru, was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sho-dynasty">Second Shō dynasty</a> of the Ryukyu Kingdom. A man of humble origins from Izena Island, he rose to become royal treasurer, and after the death of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-toku">Shō Toku</a> in 1469 he was chosen king, reigning from 1470 to 1476. His dynasty ruled Ryukyu until 1879, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-shin">Shō Shin</a> brought the kingdom to its height.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sho-en.jpg" alt="Shō En" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sho Genko, 1748-1841 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Sho_En.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
